WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.920
Speaker 1: Early last week or middle of last&nbsp;
week, I came to you and I told you that Donald&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:09.040
Trump is now conducting a frantic and frenetic&nbsp;
search for criminal defense attorneys. Why? Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:14.240
he and others increasingly believe that an&nbsp;
indictment criminally is at least a real&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:18.720
possibility, real enough that he truly needs&nbsp;
to have criminal defense attorneys ready to go.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:22.560
It appears as though that search is not going&nbsp;
particularly well, and there's a few reasons for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:28.000
that. As The Washington Post reports, Trump is&nbsp;
rushing to hire seasoned lawyers, but he keeps&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:35.440
hearing no. This is just an unbelievable line.&nbsp;
The former president's current legal team includes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:43.520
a Florida insurance lawyer who's never had&nbsp;
a federal case, a past general counsel for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:52.080
a parking garage company and a former host at&nbsp;
far right One America News. Can you imagine that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:58.160
as the former president of the United States,&nbsp;
this is the struggle that you are experiencing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:04.160
He is rushing to assemble a team of respected&nbsp;
lawyers, but the answer they keep hearing is no.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:10.720
The struggle to find expert legal advice puts&nbsp;
Trump in a bind as he faces potential criminal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:16.000
exposure from a records dispute with the National&nbsp;
Archives. Everyone is saying no, said a prominent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:20.960
Republican lawyer who, like some others, spoke on&nbsp;
the condition of anonymity to discuss confidential&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:26.800
conversations. Longtime confidence and advisers&nbsp;
of Trump have grown worried about Trump's current&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:31.280
stable of lawyers, noting most of them have&nbsp;
little to no experience in cases of this type,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:35.120
according to two people familiar with the&nbsp;
discussions. Taylor Boudreaux, which Trump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:39.840
spokesman, defended the quality of the former&nbsp;
president's legal team in a statement Tuesday.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:46.000
But it is not particularly good. John Sale, a&nbsp;
prominent Florida defense attorney who worked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:49.680
on the Watergate prosecution team, said he&nbsp;
turned down representing Trump because he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:54.240
didn't have enough time. You have to evaluate&nbsp;
whether you want to take it. It's not like a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:59.440
DUI. It's representing the former president of the&nbsp;
U.S. and maybe the next one in what's one of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:07.360
highest visibility cases ever. So normally, as&nbsp;
the article says, it's prestigious and creates&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:13.760
a lot of publicity when you represent a former&nbsp;
president. But this is a very different situation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:19.120
and we have to be able to kind of just say we know&nbsp;
what's going on here. Right. I mean, big picture,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:23.120
look at what has happened to the people&nbsp;
that defend Trump. You end up disbarred.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:29.280
You end up subpoenaed. You end up indicted. You're&nbsp;
left with an unpaid legal bill. At the end of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:35.520
day, you become ridiculed. I mean, Sidney Powell,&nbsp;
I am sure, and Sidney Powell is probably wackier&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:39.840
than the people that they've been trying to get&nbsp;
to represent Trump. Sidney Powell, I'm sure,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:46.240
believed this is my ticket to legal fame. This&nbsp;
is my ticket to legal riches. I'm going to get so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:51.920
many clients and it'll be so prestigious and the&nbsp;
PR will be great. And then she starts going around&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:57.520
with Rudy Giuliani and doing these completely&nbsp;
humiliate, humiliating appearances everywhere.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.520 --> 00:03:01.040
And she ends up disbarred. And I think it&nbsp;
was New York and D.C., I don't remember. Off&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:05.200
the top of my head, it doesn't go particularly&nbsp;
well. Look at what happened to Michael Cohen.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:08.720
Look at what happened to Giuliani,&nbsp;
Sidney Powell, I mentioned and others of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:14.800
Eric. I forget the guy's last name and all these&nbsp;
different people who have represented Trump. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:21.360
doesn't go well and he often doesn't pay. Now,&nbsp;
we learned that the Republican National Committee&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:26.400
has been paying some of Trump's legal bills for&nbsp;
a period of time. And we talked about why when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:31.840
we discuss that. But it is not a guarantee&nbsp;
that you will even be paid for your work.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:38.720
Remember the story about one of the law firms&nbsp;
that Trump had representing him years ago? They&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:44.560
would always send to people whenever they had a&nbsp;
meeting because Trump would often lie about what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:50.160
he said to his own attorneys in previous meetings.&nbsp;
So they wanted two people there so that they could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:54.720
counter the falsehoods and correct the lies. These&nbsp;
were confidential meetings with his own lawyers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.720 --> 00:04:00.000
and Trump would still lie. And of course, as a&nbsp;
more general thing in representing Trump, one of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:05.760
the biggest problems with him as a client is he&nbsp;
can't just shut up. He can't just say nothing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:09.680
And if you think back to the Russia probe, the&nbsp;
Mueller probe, whatever you want to call it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:17.360
if Trump had never said anything and not attempted&nbsp;
to obstruct or tamper with witnesses or any of it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:23.520
Trump just said, I am busy being president. I&nbsp;
will allow the investigation to run its course.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:27.280
It would have been over much faster and&nbsp;
Trump would have been under much less&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:33.360
legal jeopardy. And so it's hilarious.&nbsp;
Typically, representing a former president&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:37.840
would be a tremendously prestigious and great&nbsp;
thing to do and lucrative. But it seems like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:41.520
representing Trump is none of those things&nbsp;
and couldn't have happened to a nicer guy.

